        "visual": "01_objective_and_inferred_sources",
        "narration_source": "Choose an illustrative objective and infer image dimensions. Source labels distinguish the chosen objective, default camera assumptions, and calculated pixel spacing and Gaussian width. These values are not an optical calibration of this field."
      },
      {
        "visual": "01b_explicit_optics_source_labels",
        "narration_source": "The expanded optics panel identifies where each value came from. Calculated spacing and Gaussian width use the chosen objective and default camera or wavelength assumptions. They do not establish measured optical resolution."
      },
      {
        "visual": "02_compare_raw_and_convolved",
        "narration_source": "Compare the original with Gaussian convolution. Convolution adds blur; this is a controlled processing demonstration, not restored resolution. Richardson–Lucy is a separate option that can amplify noise."
      },
      {
        "visual": "03_apply_convolution_for_display_and_detection",
        "narration_source": "Apply enables this chain for display and detection. The source image and object labels stay unchanged."
      },
      {
        "visual": "04_return_to_original",
        "narration_source": "Switch Apply off to return to the original pixels. This editor choice does not change the intensities used by Measure."
      },
      {
        "visual": "05_measure_original_intensities",
        "narration_source": "Measure defaults to original intensities. Stored PSF settings are ignored in this mode."
      },
      {
        "visual": "06_measure_explicit_processed_intensities",
        "narration_source": "Processed intensities opt into a calibrated PSF before quantitative features. Enter explicit image sampling and kernel width; these numbers are illustrative. Stored images and exported crops retain their behavior. This lesson configures a plan without running measurement. Mask generation and Timelapse PSF settings are alpha; the editor and Measure controls shown here are available with alpha off."
      }
